{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-4-6", "id": "msg_vrtx_01JbiT1xKAo4q1k9rE82wT9K", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Step 1 validated, Step 2 loaded. Now evaluating the skill against all 14 patterns and preparing the enhancement.\n\n### Steps Executed\n- Step 1: Input Handling, completed\n- Step 2: Load Knowledge, completed\n- Step 3: Baseline Evaluation, completed\n- Step 4: Already-Optimal Detection, not optimal, continued\n- Step 5: Enhancement Targeting, completed, 11 targets selected (6 absent, 5 present)\n- Step 6: Rewrite, completed\n- Step 7: File Splitting, skipped (under 500 lines)\n- Step 8: Prompt Plugin Delegation, skipped (plugin not available)\n- Step 9: Changelog, in progress\n\n## Enhanced Skill\n\n```markdown\n---\nname: \"license:insert\"\ndescription: \"Insert license headers into source files. Use when adding copyright/license headers, stamping files with a license, or applying license boilerplate to a codebase. Do NOT use for license compliance checking, dependency license auditing, or LICENSE file generation.\"\nargument-hint: \"<directory> [--license <type>]\"\nuser-invocable: true\nallowed-tools:\n  - Read\n  - Edit\n  - Glob\n---\n\n# License Header Inserter\n\nInsert a license header at the top of all source files in a directory.\n\n## Procedure\n\n### Step 1: Resolve Inputs\n\nParse the user's input for:\n- **directory** (required): Path to scan for source files.\n- **license** (optional): License type. Defaults to \"Apache-2.0\". Supported: Apache-2.0, MIT, GPL-3.0.\n\nIf the directory does not exist, return an error and stop.\n\n### Step 2: Find Source Files\n\nUse Glob to find files matching these extensions, which cover the most common open-source project languages:\n\n```\nGlob: <directory>/**/*.{py,js,ts,go,java,rb,rs}\n```\n\nIf no files are found, report \"No source files found in `<directory>`\" and stop.\n\n### Step 3: Generate Header\n\nBuild the license header text based on the selected license type. Use comment syntax appropriate to the file extension:\n- `#` for Python, Ruby\n- `//` for JavaScript, TypeScript, Go, Rust, Java\n\nPlace a blank line after the header block so it visually separates from the file's content.\n\n### Step 4: Preview Changes\n\nBefore modifying any files, present the user with a summary of what will change:\n\n```\n## Proposed License Header Insertion\n\n**Directory**: `<path>`\n**License**: <type>\n**Files to modify**: <count>\n**Already have headers**: <count> (will be skipped)\n\n### Header to insert\n\n<formatted header text>\n\nProceed with insertion? (yes/no)\n```\n\nWait for user approval before continuing. This step exists because header insertion modifies every matched file and is tedious to reverse manually.\n\n### Step 5: Insert Headers\n\nFor each file found in Step 2, read the file and check whether it already has a license header (look for \"Copyright\" or \"License\" in the first 5 lines). If a header exists, skip that file.\n\nIf no header exists, use the Edit tool to insert the header at the top of the file.\n\nWhen inserting into Python or Ruby files, check whether the first line is a shebang (`#!`). If so, insert the header after the shebang line, not before it. Placing a header above a shebang breaks script execution.\n\n### Step 6: Verify\n\nAfter all insertions, re-read the first 10 lines of each modified file to confirm the header is present and correctly formatted. If any file's header is missing or malformed, report it as a warning in the final output. Do not retry automatically, since malformed insertions may need manual review.\n\n### Step 7: Report\n\n```\n## License Headers Inserted\n\n**Directory**: `<path>`\n**License**: <type>\n**Files scanned**: <total>\n**Headers added**: <count>\n**Already had headers**: <count>\n**Errors**: <count, or \"none\">\n```\n\n**Example output** for a typical run:\n\n```\n## License Headers Inserted\n\n**Directory**: `src/`\n**License**: Apache-2.0\n**Files scanned**: 42\n**Headers added**: 38\n**Already had headers**: 4\n**Errors**: none\n```\n\n## Error Handling\n\n| Condition | Response |\n|-----------|----------|\n| Directory not found | \"Error: Directory `<path>` not found.\" Stop. |\n| No source files found | \"No source files found in `<directory>`.\" Stop. |\n| Unsupported license type | \"Error: Unsupported license `<type>`. Supported: Apache-2.0, MIT, GPL-3.0.\" Stop. |\n| User declines preview | \"No changes made.\" Stop. |\n| Verification finds malformed header | List affected files as warnings in the report. |\n```\n\n---\n\n## What Changed\n\n| Pattern Applied | What was added/changed | Why |\n|----------------|----------------------|-----|\n| Activation Metadata | Rewrote description with trigger phrases (\"adding copyright/license headers\", \"stamping files\", \"applying license boilerplate\") | Original description was generic; new version helps Claude route correctly |\n| Exclusion Clause | Added \"Do NOT use for license compliance checking, dependency license auditing, or LICENSE file generation\" to description | These are the most likely misroutes for a license-related skill |\n| Explain-the-Why | Added rationale for file extensions, blank line after header, why preview is needed, why shebang must be preserved | Bare imperatives left Claude unable to handle edge cases |\n| Known Gotchas | Added inline shebang warning in Step 5 | Inserting a header above a shebang is the #1 mistake in license header tools |\n| Plan-Validate-Execute | Added Step 4 (Preview Changes) with user approval gate before any file modification | Original skill modified all files without confirmation, making mistakes hard to reverse |\n| Self-Correcting Loop | Added Step 6 (Verify) to re-read modified files and confirm headers are present | Without verification, silent Edit failures would go undetected |\n| In-Skill Examples | Added filled example output in Step 7 | Input/output mapping for the report format was not demonstrated |\n| Template Scaffold | Added concrete example alongside the report template | Template had placeholders but no filled demonstration |\n| Control Tuning | Made Step 2 halt on empty results; tightened Step 5 with shebang branching logic | Several steps lacked clear completion/halt criteria |\n| Execution Checklist | Added halt conditions at Steps 1, 2, and 4; renumbered to reflect new steps | Steps lacked explicit stop points for failure cases |\n| Autonomy Calibration | Added explicit user approval gate at Step 4 matching the file-modification risk profile | Skill modifies many files but had no approval checkpoint |\n\n## Status Change\n\n| Pattern | Before | After |\n|---------|--------|-------|\n| Activation Metadata | present | strong |\n| Exclusion Clause | absent | strong |\n| Control Tuning | present | strong |\n| Explain-the-Why | absent | strong |\n| Template Scaffold | present | strong |\n| In-Skill Examples | absent | strong |\n| Known Gotchas | absent | strong |\n| Execution Checklist | present | strong |\n| Self-Correcting Loop | absent | strong |\n| Plan-Validate-Execute | absent | strong |\n| Autonomy Calibration | present | strong |\n\n**Summary**: 11 patterns improved, 0 new files proposed"}], "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 4210, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 884, "cache_read_input_tokens": 37493, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 884, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 11}, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "4c4767ad-1c66-4f42-8c82-08ba4827ff3e", "uuid": "3d561f9e-91cb-47fc-9bc2-670bc57f5364", "timestamp": "2026-05-13T10:12:20.396Z"}
